cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the code, figures, or numerical experiments in this repository,
  please cite the accompanying paper listed in preferred-citation.
type: software
repository-code: 'https://github.com/PierreGuilbertF/fisher-rao-wasserstein-atlas'
title: 'Fisher–Rao and Wasserstein–Otto: A Comparative Atlas — Scripts and Figures'
authors:
  - family-names: Guilbert
    given-names: Pierre
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0002-1582-4435'
abstract: >-
  Python scripts, numerical experiments, and figures accompanying a comparative
  atlas of the pullback Fisher–Rao and Wasserstein–Otto geometries of parametric
  probability families. The examples cover location–scale, multivariate Gaussian,
  linear and nonlinear Gibbs, and push-forward families, with illustrations of
  metric costs, distances, geodesics, and transport velocity fields.
keywords:
  - Information geometry
  - Fisher–Rao metric
  - Wasserstein–Otto metric
  - Quadratic optimal transport
  - Pullback Riemannian metrics
  - Statistical manifolds
  - Location–scale families
  - Gaussian distributions
  - Bures–Wasserstein geometry
  - Gibbs families
  - Push-forward families
  - Geodesics
preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: >-
    Fisher–Rao and Wasserstein–Otto Geometries of Parametric Probability Families:
    A Comparative Atlas
  authors:
    - family-names: Guilbert
      given-names: Pierre
      orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0002-1582-4435'
  year: 2026
  notes: Preprint.
